{"title":"2003 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After his first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tests, Paul has an average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c6169a64f8271966651402df19345f38ae0c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What will his average be if he scores <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> on his next test?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find out his new average, we can first find the new total test marks and divide it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the new number of tests.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the total number of marks before his next test. Using his current average, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a89cff4a4ec438874d932dd9ed5a09f25fc93f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{6} = 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d4974c2ec12b2791c7a082cb5e6043fdf02b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 86 \\times 6 = 516$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We then see that his new total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dc7198b8e2196dc5bfcf64b2b000dc90269fe92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 100 = 516 + 100 = 616$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to calculate the new average, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9551c03d09f386500ef8b6810a6c19b758f96b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{616}{7} = \\boxed{88}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017120428\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.006 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 41/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1801/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35020:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017120428 and revision id 271932. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}